  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-06-20T06:09:30.401Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "A Global Collider literally interacts with every PB collider, but I think there are cases where we'd want to narrow down the targets to some extent. (I'm glad to see that the most notable Allow Self issue is apparently expected to be resolved by https://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/sdk-3104-beta-2-allows-us-to-ignore-a-global-collider-locally .)\n\nThis is especially apparent with inside colliders. In the current implementation, they attract absolutely everything, which means they're only really useful for creating vacuum-cleaner-style joke gimmicks. However, if the affected targets could be filtered by tags, similar to Contacts, I think it would enable the creation of much more interesting gimmicks.\n\nja:\n\nタグ付けされたGlobal Collider\n\nGlobal Colliderは文字通り全てのPB colliderに接触しますが、ある程度対象を絞りたい場合があると思います。（最も顕著なAllow Self問題は https://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/sdk-3104-beta-2-allows-us-to-ignore-a-global-collider-locally で解決される見込みのようで嬉しいです）\n\nとくにinside colliderに顕著で、現状何でも引き寄せてしまうこれは掃除機ジョークギミックを作ることくらいしかできませんが、対象をcontactsのようにタグで絞るように出来ればより面白いギミックが作れるのではないかと思います。",
